WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
Two furniture factories.

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.740
One has 20 workers.

3
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.690
The other has just 10.

4
00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.610
The big one makes 1,000 chairs a week.

5
00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.870
The small one makes 600.

6
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.310
Which factory is really doing better?

7
00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.130
It depends on what you count.

8
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:19.110
And how can the same workers make
more without working longer hours,

9
00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.850
and why does it matter?

10
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.510
In this mission, you'll tell
production apart from productivity,

11
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:26.090
and calculate both.

12
00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:29.010
Then you'll change wages
and output per worker,

13
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.630
and watch the labour cost of each unit.

14
00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.470
Your mission: find out what
lets each worker produce more.
